# <%= @title %>

Generated with `izen new`. A lightweight [Roda](https://roda.jeremyevans.net/)
app on top of the Izen core (SQLite, no ORM, no autoloader).

## Setup

```sh
bundle install
cp .env.example .env
bundle exec izen migration migrate
bundle exec izen dev
```

`izen dev` boots the Rack/Puma development server on port 3000. Pass
`--port PORT` / `--host HOST` to change the bind address.

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `app.rb` | Roda application (routes live here) |
| `app/` | Domain modules (`model`, `contract`, `repository`, `controller`) |
| `views/` | ERB templates |
| `migrations/` | Versioned up/down SQL migrations |
| `config/database.yaml` | SQLite path per `APP_ENV` |
| `storage/` | SQLite databases and the session secret |
| `config/deploy.yml` | Kamal deploy config (git-ignored) |
| `.kamal/` | Kamal secrets (git-ignored) |
| `native/` | Generated Spinel native project (`izen native build`) |

## Adding a module

```sh
bundle exec izen module new post title:string body:text
bundle exec izen migration migrate
```

## Tests

```sh
bundle exec rake test
```

## Deploy (Kamal)

`izen new` scaffolds `config/deploy.yml` and `.kamal/secrets` for a
[Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org) deploy. Fill in the placeholder server, host
and image, export the secrets, then build and ship the native binary:

```sh
bundle exec izen native build
cd native
export SESSION_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
export APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
kamal setup      # first time
kamal deploy     # afterwards
```

`izen native build` lowers the app to a [Spinel](https://github.com/matz/spinel)
project in `native/` — one native binary, no interpreter, no Rack, no Puma — and
copies `config/deploy.yml` into it (patching the proxy port to 3000). The SQLite
database and the session secret live on the `<%= @name %>_storage` volume mounted
at `/app/storage`, so redeploys keep their data.

`config/deploy.yml` and `.kamal/` are git-ignored locally: they hold server
details and secrets, so keep them on disk rather than in the repository.
